        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays' first half ended not with a roar, but with a whimper, as <strong>they fell to the Padres 5-4 on Sunday, capping a sloppy 2-game loss streak that left them at 45-51 and 12 games behind in the AL East</strong>. Coming out of the All-Star break, the clock is ticking loudly on a team that entered the break hitting just.244 and sitting 27th in runs per game. Dylan Cease, the lone bright spot, has been a force with a 2.56 ERA and 148 strikeouts in 98 innings, including a dominant All-Star shutout performance. But the bullpen and offense have been inconsistent, and the Wild Card race is begging for someone to take charge while the Jays sit on the outside edge with only 20.6% playoff odds. <strong>Friday's 7:15 PM ET matchup against the White Sox at home offers a chance to break the skid and reset the trajectory</strong>.",
